        "id": "p35-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Which box plot do you think is before her ride and which is after? Explain with reference to clustering.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Top: before the ride. Bottom: after the ride. The middle 50% shifts from 74–86 bpm to 86–98 bpm.",
          "worked": "The top plot is before the ride and the bottom plot is after. The middle 50% of readings lies between 74 and 86 bpm in the top plot, compared with 86 and 98 bpm in the bottom plot. This cluster has shifted to higher heart rates, as expected after exercise.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Compare her IQR before and after a ride. Does her heartrate remain consistent?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both IQRs are 12 bpm. The variability of the middle 50% remains the same, although her heart rate increases.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{IQR before}&=86-74\\\\&=12\\text{ bpm}\\\\\\text{IQR after}&=98-86\\\\&=12\\text{ bpm}\\end{aligned}$$\nHer heart rate remains consistent in terms of the spread of the middle 50% of readings. The readings shift to higher values after the ride, so the heart rate itself has increased.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
